<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Ecosystem Courtroom</title><style>
*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:radial-gradient(ellipse at top,#39434b,#131b23);color:#f5efdf;font:clamp(16px,2vw,24px)/1.5 system-ui;min-height:100vh}header{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;padding:16px 4%;border-bottom:2px solid #b99a61;background:#17212b}small,.eyebrow{font-size:.65em;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#d4bd89}h1,h2,h3{font-family:Georgia,serif;line-height:1.15;margin:.4em 0}h1{font-size:clamp(25px,4vw,48px)}h2{font-size:clamp(28px,4vw,54px)}main{max-width:1200px;margin:auto;padding:25px 4%}button{font:inherit;cursor:pointer;border:1px solid #b99a61;border-radius:7px;background:#263745;color:#fff;padding:.55em 1em}button:hover,button:focus-visible{background:#496071;outline:2px solid #e8ca8e}button:disabled{opacity:.4;cursor:default}.gold{background:#c6a66c;color:#17212b;font-weight:700}.paper{background:#f6f0e3;color:#292d30;border-radius:10px;padding:clamp(18px,3vw,36px);box-shadow:0 10px 30px #0004;border-top:5px solid #b99a61;margin:16px 0}.paper .eyebrow{color:#75613e}.docket{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(260px,1fr));gap:14px}.case{text-align:left;min-height:125px}.case strong{display:block;font:1.25em Georgia}.portrait{font-size:clamp(65px,10vw,130px);line-height:1.1}.row{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap}.nav{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:20px}.quote{font:1.35em/1.5 Georgia,serif}.prompt{border-left:4px solid #a48b56;padding:12px 18px;background:#e9e2d3;margin-top:20px}.vote{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #d4cbbb;padding:12px 0}.vote button{min-width:48px}.bar{height:15px;background:#d9d3c7;border-radius:5px;overflow:hidden;margin:5px 0 12px}.bar i{display:block;height:100%;background:#57778a}.steps{display:flex;gap:5px;margin:10px 0}.steps i{height:5px;flex:1;background:#65717b;border-radius:4px}.steps i.on{background:#d4b679}textarea{width:100%;font:inherit;padding:10px;min-height:70px}footer{font-size:12px;text-align:center;color:#b8c2c9;padding:15px}.selected{outline:3px solid #b99a61} @media(max-width:600px){header{flex-wrap:wrap}.row{gap:10px}.vote{font-size:16px}}
</style><header><div><small>Mr. Liscomb’s Science Class</small><h1>⚖ Ecosystem Courtroom</h1></div><div><button id="sound" aria-pressed="false">Sound off</button> <button id="full">Full screen</button></div></header><main id="app"></main><footer>Fictional cases • Simplified ecological scenarios • Teacher-led discussion</footer><script>
const cases=[
['Fox','🦊','Food chains and energy transfer','Reducing the rabbit population','A fox has moved into a grassland. Rabbit numbers have fallen since its arrival.','Is the fox harming the ecosystem or fulfilling an ecological role?',[
['Rabbit','🐇','Prosecution','The fox has been hunting rabbits. Our population has decreased.','How does the fox obtain energy?'],['Fox','🦊','Defendant','I cannot make my own food. I need to consume other organisms to survive.','Is the fox a producer or a consumer?'],['Grass','🌿','Surprise witness','When there were more rabbits, much of the vegetation was eaten. More grass is growing now.','How can a predator indirectly affect a producer?'],['Deer','🦌','Additional witness','There is more vegetation available for other herbivores now.','How can one feeding relationship affect other organisms?']], 'Predation harms individual prey but can limit prey populations and reduce grazing pressure. The fox obtains energy by consuming prey. Effects depend on the wider food web.','Sun → Grass → Rabbit → Fox','What might happen to rabbits, grass and deer if foxes disappeared?'],
['Mushroom','🍄','Decomposition','Breaking down a fallen tree','A dead tree is gradually breaking apart. Fungi have been found growing on its wood.','Is the fungus damaging the ecosystem or performing a necessary function?',[
['Fallen tree','🪵','Prosecution','My wood has become soft and is breaking apart.','What is happening to the dead material?'],['Mushroom','🍄','Defendant','The tree was already dead. I obtain energy by breaking down organic matter.','Why is a mushroom not a producer?'],['Seedling','🌱','Surprise witness','As dead material breaks down, nutrients become available in the soil. I can absorb them.','How does decomposition benefit plants?'],['Bacteria','🦠','Expert witness','Many bacteria also break down dead organic material.','What would happen without decomposers?']], 'Decomposers obtain energy from dead organic matter and help recycle nutrients. Matter cycles; energy flows.','Dead wood → Fungi (energy transfer)','What would a forest look like after years without decomposers?'],
['Rabbit','🐇','Limiting factors','Consuming too much vegetation','Rabbit numbers have increased and vegetation is becoming scarce.','Is the rabbit alone responsible?',[
['Grass','🌿','Prosecution','Vegetation is being eaten faster than it can regrow.','What resource is limited?'],['Rabbit','🐇','Defendant','I am a herbivore. Plants are my source of energy.','Why do herbivores depend on producers?'],['Fox','🦊','Surprise witness','Our population declined after habitat was cleared. Fewer foxes are hunting rabbits.','How might fewer predators affect prey?'],['Deer','🦌','Additional witness','We depend on some of the same plants as rabbits. Food is scarce.','How are rabbits and deer interacting?']], 'Rabbit grazing contributes to vegetation loss, but habitat change, predator numbers and food availability also influence population balance.','Fewer foxes → More rabbits → Greater grazing pressure','What may happen to rabbits if vegetation continues to decline?'],
['Beaver','🦫','Habitats and biodiversity','Flooding a forest','A dam across a stream has raised water levels and flooded nearby land.','Has the beaver damaged a habitat, created a new one, or both?',[
['Pine tree','🌲','Prosecution','Water has flooded the soil around our roots. Some trees have died.','Which abiotic condition changed?'],['Squirrel','🐿️','Prosecution','Some trees that provided shelter are no longer suitable.','How has our habitat changed?'],['Duck','🦆','Surprise witness','The new pond provides shallow water and habitat for raising young.','Why might ducks benefit?'],['Frog','🐸','Additional witness','The pond provides water for our eggs and developing young.','Can one change help some species and harm others?']], 'Beaver dams modify habitats. Flooding can harm terrestrial organisms while creating wetland habitat for others. Effects depend on local conditions.','Stream → Beaver dam → Wetland habitat','How might the types of organisms here change over time?'],
['Bee','🐝','Interdependence','Taking nectar from flowers','A bee repeatedly visits flowers and removes nectar.','Are both organisms benefiting?',[
['Flower','🌻','Prosecution','The bee removes nectar from my flowers.','What resource is being taken?'],['Bee','🐝','Defendant','Nectar contains sugars that provide energy.','How does energy move from plant to bee?'],['Nearby flower','🌼','Surprise witness','The bee carries pollen between flowers, helping us reproduce.','What benefit can plants receive?'],['Bird','🐦','Additional witness','Some pollinated plants produce seeds and fruit that we eat.','How can pollination affect the food web?']], 'Many flowering plants and pollinators have a mutually beneficial relationship. Bees obtain food and pollen transfer can help plants reproduce.','Flower provides food ↔ Bee transfers pollen','How could fewer pollinators affect other organisms?'],
['Zebra mussel','🐚','Invasive species','Disrupting a lake ecosystem','Zebra mussels have been introduced outside their native range and have spread through a lake.','What causes the harm, and how should humans respond?',[
['Native mussel','🐚','Prosecution','Zebra mussels attach to our shells and interfere with feeding and movement.','How are native organisms affected?'],['Fish','🐟','Prosecution','The mussels filter tiny organisms from the water, changing food availability.','How can competition affect food webs?'],['Zebra mussel','🐚','Defendant','I feed and reproduce as I would in my native habitat. I did not choose to be transported here.','Why does ecological context matter?'],['Conservation officer','🚤','Surprise witness','Human activities can transport invasive species. Cleaning, draining and drying equipment can help prevent spread.','What can humans do?']], 'Zebra mussels can harm native species and alter food webs outside their native range. Preventing further introductions is an important human responsibility.','Human transport → Introduction → Spread → Impacts','How could people protect local lakes?'],
['Farmer','🚜','Human impacts','Contributing to an algal bloom','After heavy rain, nutrients entered a lake near farmland. A large algal bloom developed.','How should the community respond?',[
['Fish','🐟','Prosecution','As the bloom decayed, oxygen levels fell and some fish struggled to survive.','Why is dissolved oxygen important?'],['Farmer','🧑‍🌾','Defendant','Crops need nutrients. Some fertilizer may have been carried away by rain.','Why do farmers add nutrients?'],['Decomposer','🦠','Expert witness','Microorganisms break down dead algae, consuming dissolved oxygen.','How does decomposition affect oxygen?'],['Environmental scientist','🌿','Surprise witness','Vegetated buffer strips and careful fertilizer management can reduce runoff.','Can farming continue while reducing harm?']], 'Excess nutrients can promote algal blooms. Decomposition can reduce dissolved oxygen. Multiple nutrient sources may contribute; management should follow evidence.','Runoff → Algal bloom → Decomposition → Lower oxygen','Propose a solution that considers both farming and the lake.']];
let c=-1,p=0,votes=[[0,0,0],[0,0,0]],notes=['',''],verdict='',sound=false,heard=new Set();const app=document.querySelector('#app'),labels=['Guilty','Not guilty','Undecided'],steps=['Charges','Witness A','Witness B','Initial vote','Witness C','Witness D','Arguments','Final vote','Judgment'];const esc=s=>String(s).replace(/[&<>"']/g,x=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#39;'}[x]));
function gavel(){if(!sound)return;try{let a=new (window.AudioContext||window.webkitAudioContext)(),o=a.createOscillator(),g=a.createGain();o.type='triangle';o.frequency.setValueAtTime(140,a.currentTime);o.frequency.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(45,a.currentTime+.12);g.gain.setValueAtTime(.3,a.currentTime);g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(.001,a.currentTime+.16);o.connect(g);g.connect(a.destination);o.start();o.stop(a.currentTime+.17);o.onended=()=>a.close()}catch(e){}}
function openCase(i){c=i;p=0;votes=[[0,0,0],[0,0,0]];notes=['',''];verdict='';gavel();render()}
function move(n){p=Math.max(0,Math.min(8,p+n));gavel();render();window.scrollTo(0,0)}
function render(){if(c<0){app.innerHTML='<div class="eyebrow">Case docket</div><h2>Select a case</h2><p>Choose a trial. Hear the evidence, deliberate and deliver a verdict.</p><div class="docket">'+cases.map((a,i)=>`<button class="case" data-case="${i}"><small>Case ${String(i+1).padStart(3,'0')}${heard.has(i)?' · Heard':''}</small><strong>${a[1]} The People v. The ${a[0]}</strong>${a[2]}</button>`).join('')+'</div>';return}let a=cases[c],html=`<div class="eyebrow">Case ${String(c+1).padStart(3,'0')} · ${steps[p]}</div><div class="steps">${steps.map((_,i)=>`<i class="${i<=p?'on':''}"></i>`).join('')}</div>`;
if(p===0)html+=`<section class="paper"><div class="row"><div class="portrait">${a[1]}</div><div><div class="eyebrow">Defendant</div><h2>The People v. The ${a[0]}</h2><h3>Charge: ${a[3]}</h3></div></div><p>${a[4]}</p><div class="prompt">${a[5]}</div></section>`;
if([1,2,4,5].includes(p)){let i=[1,2,4,5].indexOf(p),w=a[6][i];html+=`<section class="paper"><div class="eyebrow">Exhibit ${'ABCD'[i]} · ${w[2]}</div><div class="row"><div class="portrait">${w[1]}</div><h2>${w[0]}</h2></div><div class="quote">“${w[3]}”</div><div class="prompt"><b>Question for the court</b><br>${w[4]}</div></section>`}
if(p===3||p===7){let k=p===3?0:1;html+=`<section class="paper"><h2>${p===3?'Initial':'Final'} jury vote</h2><p>${p===3?'Based on the evidence so far, what is your position?':'Consider all the evidence. Has your position changed?'}</p>${labels.map((l,i)=>`<div class="vote"><b>${l}</b><div class="row"><button data-vote="${i}" data-delta="-1" aria-label="Remove ${l} vote">−</button><strong>${votes[k][i]}</strong><button data-vote="${i}" data-delta="1" aria-label="Add ${l} vote">+</button></div></div>`).join('')}<p>${votes[k].reduce((x,y)=>x+y,0)} votes recorded. Teacher enters tally; recording is optional.</p></section>`}
if(p===6)html+=`<section class="paper"><h2>Closing arguments</h2><h3>Prosecution</h3><p>What negative effects has the defendant had? Cite evidence.</p><textarea data-note="0" placeholder="Optional notes">${esc(notes[0])}</textarea><h3>Defence</h3><p>What ecological role or other factors should be considered? Cite evidence.</p><textarea data-note="1" placeholder="Optional notes">${esc(notes[1])}</textarea><div class="prompt">Jury: Which arguments are supported by the strongest evidence?</div></section>`;
if(p===8)html+=`<section class="paper"><h2>Judgment of the court</h2><h3>Initial and final votes</h3>${labels.map((l,i)=>`<b>${l}</b>${votes.map((v,k)=>`<div>${k?'Final':'Initial'}: ${v[i]} / ${v.reduce((x,y)=>x+y,0)}</div><div class="bar"><i style="width:${100*v[i]/Math.max(1,v.reduce((x,y)=>x+y,0))}%;opacity:${k?1:.5}"></i></div>`).join('')}`).join('')}<h3>Record the class verdict</h3><div class="row">${['Guilty','Not guilty','Complex outcome'].map(v=>`<button data-verdict="${v}" class="${verdict===v?'selected':''}">${v}</button>`).join('')}</div>${verdict?`<p><b>Verdict: ${verdict}</b></p>`:''}<h3>Scientific findings</h3><p>${a[7]}</p><div class="prompt">${a[8]}</div><h3>Final question</h3><p>${a[9]}</p></section>`;
html+=`<div class="nav"><button id="docket">Case docket</button>${p?'<button id="back">← Back</button>':''}<button class="gold" id="next">${['Call first witness','Call next witness','Initial vote','Reveal new evidence','Call next witness','Closing arguments','Final vote','Deliver judgment','Adjourn case'][p]} →</button></div>`;app.innerHTML=html}
app.addEventListener('click',e=>{let b=e.target.closest('button');if(!b)return;if(b.dataset.case!==undefined)openCase(+b.dataset.case);else if(b.id==='next'){if(p===8){heard.add(c);c=-1;gavel();render()}else move(1)}else if(b.id==='back')move(-1);else if(b.id==='docket'){if(confirm('Return to docket? Current trial votes and notes will be cleared when reopened.')){c=-1;render()}}else if(b.dataset.vote!==undefined){let v=votes[p===3?0:1],i=+b.dataset.vote;v[i]=Math.max(0,v[i]+ +b.dataset.delta);render()}else if(b.dataset.verdict){verdict=b.dataset.verdict;render()}});app.addEventListener('input',e=>{if(e.target.dataset.note!==undefined)notes[+e.target.dataset.note]=e.target.value});document.querySelector('#full').onclick=async()=>{try{if(document.fullscreenElement)await document.exitFullscreen();else await document.documentElement.requestFullscreen()}catch(e){alert('Full screen is unavailable in this browser. Try F11.')}};document.querySelector('#sound').onclick=e=>{sound=!sound;e.target.textContent=sound?'Sound on':'Sound off';e.target.setAttribute('aria-pressed',sound);gavel()};document.addEventListener('keydown',e=>{if(c<0||['TEXTAREA','INPUT','BUTTON'].includes(document.activeElement.tagName))return;if(e.key==='ArrowRight'&&p<8){e.preventDefault();move(1)}if(e.key==='ArrowLeft'&&p>0){e.preventDefault();move(-1)}});render();
</script></html>
